-- title:
--   An element of density at least $7/18$
-- statement:
--   **The rung $r=7$ of the scaled union-closed sets conjecture.** Every finite union-closed family $\mathcal F$ of finite sets with $\mathcal F\ne\emptyset$ and $\mathcal F\ne\{\emptyset\}$ has an element of density at least $\tfrac12-\tfrac19$:
--
--   $$\exists x:\quad \delta_{\mathcal F}(x)\ \ge\ \frac7{18} .$$
--
--   This rung is open.
-- source:
--   Open; the best published constants are slightly above $0.382$, e.g. J. Liu, Improving the lower bound for the union-closed sets conjecture via conditionally IID coupling, https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.08824

